# V3.902 — browsers ask before reusing a page, script or stylesheet under /rm/.
# The host sends no Cache-Control, so a browser kept its own copy for ~10% of
# the file's age without asking: after a deploy, RM and the notebook's Scientia
# iframe could open the previous version for half an hour, or for days when the
# file had not changed in weeks. "no-cache" = check every time; an unchanged
# file comes back as a 304 of a few hundred bytes (ETag / Last-Modified).
# Images, PDFs and fonts keep normal caching. sw.js does the same for its own
# fetches (revalidating()), which also reaches copies saved before this file.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.(html?|js|mjs|css|json|webmanifest)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache"
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
